    // (anon-function 21 joint-mod): a compiler-generated trampoline for
    // storing joint-mod-foot-rot-handler (declared with a :behavior process
    // tag) into a cspace param0 slot; the trampoline itself is a 0-arg
    // stub that tail-calls the real handler through a0/a1 without ever
    // setting them, so type analysis reports both as read-but-unset. The
    // real handler (joint-mod-foot-rot-handler, typed via this file's own
    // type_casts.jsonc entry) decompiles cleanly; this wrapper carries no
    // logic of its own to recover. Parked as asm.
    "(anon-function 21 joint-mod)",
    // joint-mod-ik-callback: a large (400+ op) two-bone IK solver. Once its
    // gp/joint-mod-ik casts are applied (type_casts.jsonc) it fails on a
    // single remaining register, s5, which is reused across the whole
    // function body as a rolling base pointer into roughly two dozen stack
    // slots (offsets 16 through 752, jak3's twin at
    // decompiler/config/jak3/ntsc_v1/stack_structures.jsonc:58 declares all
    // of them) rather than being re-derived fresh from sp at each site, the
    // way collide-planes's own multi-slot stack base is. Typing s5 as its
    // first declared slot (matrix, offset 16) breaks every later offset
    // past that type's own size ("add failed: matrix <integer 208>");
    // forcing a raw pointer type through the whole span (tried (pointer
    // int32), then (pointer vector)) clears the type-prop errors but
    // produces implausible scaled offsets in the pretty-printed source
    // (index 52 where the raw byte offset is 208), evidence the cast changes
    // what the decompiler infers rather than just permitting the arithmetic.
    // jak3 needs no equivalent cast for its own twin, so this is jakx-only
    // codegen, and no evidence in this band distinguishes a genuinely
    // correct wide pointer type from one that merely silences the checker.
    // Parked as asm rather than risk a plausible-but-wrong decode; referenced
    // only through the type's own callback field, never embedded inline as
    // data.
    "joint-mod-ik-callback",
    // powerup-draw-method-53 (time-freeze-short-draw/long-draw/med-draw
    // overrides): raw, unconverted register dump; a1/a2 are declared
    // generic object per all-types.gc with no call-site evidence in this
    // band for their real types (no caller of this method decodes within
    // time-box-obs itself), so retyping them would be a guess. Parked as
    // asm; referenced only through the type's own vtable dispatch, never
    // embedded inline as data.
    "(method 53 time-freeze-short-draw)",
    "(method 53 time-freeze-long-draw)",
    "(method 53 time-freeze-med-draw)",
    // powerup-draw-method-54 (same three overrides): a large part-tracker/
    // debris-spawn handler; adding the missing _type_ arg0 (all-types.gc)
    // got it much further (op 5 to op 94) but it still fails on a 112-byte
    // stack structure and a process root-field read this band has no
    // further evidence for (a vehicle-handle uint64 -> handle retype was
    // tried and made no difference, reverted). Parked as asm.
    "(method 54 time-freeze-short-draw)",
    "(method 54 time-freeze-long-draw)",
    "(method 54 time-freeze-med-draw)",
    // net-powerup-method-50/52 (time-freeze-short override, inherited by
    // time-freeze-long/med): raw, unconverted; a1/a2 declared generic
    // object per all-types.gc (method 50) and method 52's declared single
    // process-tree arg does not account for the a2 register the body
    // actually reads, with no in-band call-site evidence for either.
    // Parked as asm.
    "(method 50 time-freeze-short)",
    "(method 52 time-freeze-short)",
    // kras-pump-break-proxy-method-61/62: both read at least one arg
    // beyond a widened (object object) guess before failing further in;
    // method 62 additionally regressed from a type-prop error to a full
    // CFG failure under a rigid-body-impact retype for its one declared
    // arg (tried and reverted, despite the arg's offset-48 float load
    // being an exact match for rigid-body-impact's own impulse field),
    // so something about this pair resists the type_casts/all-types.gc
    // route with the evidence available in this band. Parked as asm.
    "(method 61 kras-pump-break-proxy)",
    "(method 62 kras-pump-break-proxy)",
    // train-obs: six free functions with zero in-band call-site evidence
    // for their signatures (every caller also failed to decode, since
    // they cascade off the same unresolved chain), all left as bare
    // `function` externs in the pre-authored reservoir. Parked as asm
    // rather than guessed at.
    "train-car-init-by-other",
    "train-car-spawn",
    "position-train-car",
    "train-move",
    "cars-spawn",
    "play-horn",
    // (method 10 train): overrides deactivate; a2 loaded straight from a0
    // (this) with no resolvable field evidence for what it reads.
    "(method 10 train)",
    // (method 71 train): the quaternion-look-at!/quaternion->matrix
    // compound stack shape is declared (stack_structures.jsonc) but the
    // arithmetic itself still fails ("add failed: quaternion <integer
    // 64>"), the same class already fixed by hand for peak-obs but with
    // no in-band op-level evidence here for which casts to add without
    // risking the same silent-corruption failure mode already hit once
    // in this band (peak-obs's rbody-collision root cast).
    "(method 71 train)",
    // (method 66 train): full CFG failure, no error detail to act on.
    "(method 66 train)",
    // end-end-credits: reads *end-credits-proc* (handle) through a raw
    // doubleword load off its own symbol-slot address with no in-band
    // evidence for the surrounding stack shape.
    "end-end-credits",
    // title-control-init/title-control-spawn/draw-language-select: each
    // decodes to seemingly complete GOAL text ("may read a0" was the only
    // decode-time flag) but fails real compilation with a raw label leak
    // (an unresolved anon-function, e.g. L215 in title-control-init's
    // dma-get-named-buffer call) or return-type mismatches that trace back
    // to the same unresolved inner lambda; parked as asm.
    "title-control-init",
    "title-control-spawn",
    "draw-language-select",
    // desarena-obs: desarena-activate/deactivate never decoded at all
    // ("no type analysis"), no in-band call-site evidence (nothing in
    // this object calls them; they are level-hook functions referenced
    // from elsewhere, out of this band's scope).
    "desarena-activate",
    "desarena-deactivate",
    // palm-tree's own methods 11/52/54/55: all raw, unconverted register
    // dumps reading a1/uninitialized locals with no traceable source
    // (method 55: "add failed uninitialized integer 16" plus a stack-use
    // guess failure; method 54: raw l.q load; method 11 and 52: fully
    // unconverted). method 52 is called from (post idle palm-tree), which
    // still resolves fine against a parked method's decoder-generated
    // stub body.
    "(method 11 palm-tree)",
    "(method 52 palm-tree)",
    "(method 54 palm-tree)",
    "(method 55 palm-tree)",
    // palm-tree-a/b/c's own method 35 and 54 overrides (six total): the
    // same "may read a1 not set" pattern as the base type's method 54
    // (a1 is very likely a vector impact-velocity/direction argument, but
    // no in-band evidence pins the exact signature since every one of
    // these bodies reads it uninitialized rather than receiving it as a
    // declared param).
    "(method 35 palm-tree-a)",
    "(method 54 palm-tree-a)",
    "(method 35 palm-tree-b)",
    "(method 54 palm-tree-b)",
    "(method 35 palm-tree-c)",
    "(method 54 palm-tree-c)",
    // (enter explode-into-nothing wvehicle) and (enter explode wvehicle),
    // internal names (anon-function 16 wvehicle-states) and (anon-function
    // 18 wvehicle-states): asm_functions_by_name is consulted before
    // state-handler recognition renames the function, so the internal name
    // is the key that matches here (same shape as (anon-function 6
    // credits-obs) above). Both bodies build an explosion-init-params
    // struct and fully resolve (stack struct, both handle fields, the
    // ppointer-chase type prop) except for the low-level "sllv reg, reg,
    // r0" step that folds the resolved ppointer into the handle's low
    // 32 bits: the decompiler's handle idiom matcher only recognizes that
    // shift when its source is already handle-typed (the direct
    // field-load case, e.g. (post sink wvehicle)'s wheel-handle loop in
    // this same file), not when the source is a (pointer process) freshly
    // produced by a ppointer chase, which is what process->handle's own
    // inline expansion produces here. Same failure class as (method 10
    // rigid-body-queue) below (raw "sllv reg, reg, r0" triple the macro
    // matcher does not recognize); parked as asm rather than hand-folded
    // since both bodies are large (128+ and 352+ stack bytes) and the only
    // unresolved piece is this one bit-twiddle, not the surrounding logic.
    "(anon-function 16 wvehicle-states)",
    "(anon-function 18 wvehicle-states)",
    // wcar-skel-template rung (extern-no-defun keystone): get-car-skel-part
    // is a global 5-iteration search loop (format "<name>-<letter>" for
    // letter in a..e, look it up via a level vtable method, and on the
    // first hit stash the match into arg2's art-group-name field and
    // return arg2). The compiler places the found-and-break arm as the
    // loop-check branch's fallthrough (block 2 of 7) and the not-found/
    // continue arm as the taken branch (block 3, which rejoins the loop
    // test at block 4). CfgVtx.cpp's find_cond_n_else requires the block
    // right after a single-case body to be either the shared end block or
    // the start of a second cond arm whose own body block has exactly one
    // pred; block 4 has two (the initial entry jump and the continue
    // edge), so it rejects (trace: c0=block1, b0=block2, next=block3 !=
    // end_block(block6), so it tries c=block3/b=block3->next=block4 as a
    // second arm and rejects on b->pred.size()==2). find_goto_not_end
    // requires the block right after the break (block 3) to have zero
    // preds to treat it as dead fallthrough, but block 3 is live (block1's
    // own branch target), so it declines too. Every other cond/loop
    // matcher in the while(changed) driver was traced the same way and
    // none fit this shape. This is a CFG-shape gap in the pattern matcher,
    // not a missing type: all-types.gc's existing define-extern for
    // get-car-skel-part is already correct. Parked as asm; get-car-skel-part
    // stays declared via define-extern in wcar-skel-template.gc (its own
    // object) with no body, the same tradeoff as raptor.gc's
    // raptor-startup-code and race-line.gc's methods 11-14, so the ~120
    // game-DGO call sites stay unbound (e2 class) until a real fix lands
    // (a mips2c port or a CfgVtx.cpp change, both out of this rung's
    // scope). Landing wcar-skel-template's own decode does not close the
    // extern-no-defun class for this symbol.
    "get-car-skel-part"
